From: sshathee <shunmugam.shatheesh@windriver.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 04:45:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Disable LVM monitoring in initramfs

Thin pools that are auto-activated by udev in the initramfs register
with dmeventd, because activation/monitoring defaults to 1. LVM then
starts dmeventd from the initramfs. That dmeventd survives switch_root
in init.scope, outside any systemd unit, and holds /run/dmeventd.pid so
dm-event.service cannot take over. At shutdown it is not stopped in
order and systemd-shutdown can wait up to 90 seconds on it.

Set activation/monitoring to 0 in the initramfs lvm.conf when LVM is
enabled. Volume groups are still activated. lvm2-monitor.service
registers monitoring in the real root once dm-event.socket is up, so
dmeventd then runs under dm-event.service.

Signed-off-by: sshathee <shunmugam.shatheesh@windriver.com>
---
 init-ostree.sh | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/init-ostree.sh b/init-ostree.sh
index 14a5476..6d7566d 100755
--- a/init-ostree.sh
+++ b/init-ostree.sh
@@ -74,6 +74,9 @@ disable_lvm() {
 
 enable_lvm() {
 	sed -i "s#^\(\t*\)global_filter = \[.*#\1global_filter = [ \"a|.*|\" ]#" /etc/lvm/lvm.conf
+	# Do not start dmeventd in the initramfs, it would outlive switch_root
+	# outside any unit. Monitoring is enabled later in the real root.
+	sed -i "s#^\(\t*\)\# monitoring = 1#\1monitoring = 0#" /etc/lvm/lvm.conf
 }
 
 activate_multipath() {
